                <pb facs="0381" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg283"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum delivered by the Chinese
                    minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Cablegram from Yu Lien-Yuen, taotai
                        of Shanghai, received by Minister Wu on the 8th of August, 1900.</hi></p>
                <p>Have received telegram from Governor Yuan Shih-Kai to the effect that the Tsungli
                    Yamen received on the 5th of August an Imperial edict allowing all the foreign
                    ministers free communication with their respective governments in cipher.</p>
            </div>
